module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Abelian
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.FlatFppfModuleShriek

/-!
# Additivity and exactness of the flat-fppf comparison functors

Let `𝒳` be an algebraic stack over `S` and let `g : Sh(𝒳_{flat,fppf}) ⟶ Sh(𝒳_{fppf})` be the
morphism of topoi of **Stacks 0788** (2). Forming the *derived* functors `Lg_!` and `g^{-1}` on
unbounded derived categories, which is what **Stacks 07AS** asserts to exist, presupposes three
homological facts about the underived functors:

* lower shriek `g_!` on abelian sheaves is additive, so that it acts on homotopy categories;
* lower shriek `g_!` on sheaves of modules is additive, for the same reason;
* restriction `g^{-1}` on abelian sheaves is **exact**, so that it descends to unbounded derived
  categories directly, with no derived functor to construct.

All three are proved here. Each is immediate from an adjunction that is already available: `g_!`
is a left adjoint in both cases (**Stacks 0788** (2)(d) and **Stacks 0789** (2)), and a left
adjoint between preadditive categories with binary biproducts is additive; restriction is the
*right* adjoint of `g_!` and simultaneously the *left* adjoint of the cocontinuous pushforward, so
it preserves both finite limits and finite colimits.

Nothing here carries a `@[stacks]` attribute. These three statements are ingredients of
**Stacks 07AS** and not clauses of it: 07AS asserts the existence of the total left derived
functor `Lg_!`, its adjointness to `g^{-1}`, and that `g^{-1}Lg_! = id`, and its proof is
Cohomology on Sites, Lemma **07AC**, which has no rendering in this library. These are the parts
of the apparatus that do not need 07AC.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.hasSheafify_topology_ab`: abelian sheaves on the flat-fppf
  site of an algebraic stack have a sheafification, in any coefficient universe containing that of
  the schemes of the site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.abelianShriek_additive`: lower shriek on abelian sheaves is
  additive.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.abelianRestriction_exact_topology`: restriction of abelian
  sheaves along the inclusion of the flat objects is exact.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.moduleShriek_additive`: lower shriek on sheaves of modules is
  additive.

## Implementation notes

`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.hasSheafify_topology_ab` is stated here because the sheafify
instances of `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.FlatFppfInclusion` cover the ambient fppf site
only; the flat-fppf site needs its own, and it is the same argument — the site is essentially
small, so `CategoryTheory.hasSheafifyEssentiallySmallSite` applies at any larger coefficient
universe. With it the category of abelian sheaves on the flat-fppf site is abelian, hence has
binary biproducts, which is the hypothesis
`CategoryTheory.Functor.additive_of_preservesBinaryBiproducts` makes on the *source*.

The instances the three results need are the `theorem`s of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.FlatFppfInclusion` and
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.FlatFppfRingedModules` that those files themselves install
with `attribute [local instance]`; a local instance does not cross a module boundary, so they are
re-installed here. They are `theorem`s rather than `instance`s by those files' documented design:
each is a statement about one particular site rather than a general one.

`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.abelianRestriction_exact_topology` spells its functor out as
`CategoryTheory.Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuous` rather than naming it, exactly as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.abelianShriekAdjunction` does, so that no second name for
restriction is introduced.

Its name carries the `_topology` suffix of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.isContinuous_inclusion_topology`, the local instance it
consumes: the site is `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.topology`, the topology generated by
the inherited covering families, whereas
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.abelianRestriction_exact` is the same assertion at
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.inclusionTopology`, with the coefficients fixed at the
universe above the schemes. The two topologies agree by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.inclusionTopology_eq_topology`, but the categories of sheaves
they name are not the same type, so neither statement follows from the other without transport.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0788](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0788)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0789](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0789)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07AS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07AS)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf

universe u w v

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
  (𝒳 : Stack.AlgebraicStacks.{u, w} B S hS)

attribute [local instance] isContinuous_inclusion_topology isCocontinuous_inclusion_topology
  essentiallySmall_obj_coefficient essentiallySmall_flatFppf hasSheafify_associatedTopology_ab
  hasLeftKanExtension_inclusion_ab hasPointwiseRightKanExtension_inclusion_ab

/-- Abelian sheaves on the flat-fppf site of an algebraic stack have a sheafification, in any
coefficient universe containing that of the schemes of the site. This is the flat-fppf companion
of `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.hasSheafify_associatedTopology_ab`, by the same argument:
the site is essentially small. -/
theorem hasSheafify_topology_ab :
    HasSheafify (topology B S hS 𝒳) Ab.{max u v} :=
  hasSheafifyEssentiallySmallSite.{_, _, _, _, max u v} _ _

attribute [local instance] hasSheafify_topology_ab

/-- A left adjoint between preadditive categories, the source having binary biproducts, is
additive. -/
private theorem additive_of_isLeftAdjoint {C D : Type*} [Category C] [Category D] [Preadditive C]
    [Preadditive D] [HasBinaryBiproducts C] (F : C ⥤ D) [F.IsLeftAdjoint] : F.Additive := by
  have := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBinaryCoproducts F
  exact Functor.additive_of_preservesBinaryBiproducts _

/-- **Lower shriek on abelian sheaves is additive.** `g_!` of **Stacks 0788** (2)(d) is a left
adjoint, so it preserves binary coproducts, hence binary biproducts, hence is additive; the
source category is abelian because the flat-fppf site is essentially small.

This is the hypothesis under which `g_!` acts on homotopy categories of complexes, and therefore
the first thing the total left derived functor `Lg_!` of **Stacks 07AS** part (3) needs. -/
theorem abelianShriek_additive : (abelianShriek.{u, w, v} B S hS 𝒳).Additive := by
  have : (abelianShriek.{u, w, v} B S hS 𝒳).IsLeftAdjoint :=
    ⟨_, ⟨abelianShriekAdjunction.{u, w, v} B S hS 𝒳⟩⟩
  exact additive_of_isLeftAdjoint _

/-- **Restriction of abelian sheaves to the flat-fppf site is exact.** The inverse image
`g^{-1}` of the morphism of topoi of **Stacks 0788** (2)(a) has adjoints on both sides: it is the
right adjoint of `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.abelianShriek`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.abelianShriekAdjunction`), so it preserves finite limits, and
it is the left adjoint of the cocontinuous pushforward
(`CategoryTheory.Functor.sheafAdjunctionCocontinuous`), so it preserves finite colimits.

Exactness is what makes `g^{-1}` act on *unbounded* derived categories with no derived functor to
construct, through `CategoryTheory.Functor.mapDerivedCategory`; it is the hypothesis **Stacks
07AS** needs in order to state that `Lg_!` is left adjoint to derived restriction. -/
theorem abelianRestriction_exact_topology :
    exactFunctor (Sheaf (associatedTopology B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p B.topology) Ab.{max u v})
      (Sheaf (topology B S hS 𝒳) Ab.{max u v})
      ((objectProperty B S hS 𝒳).ι.sheafPushforwardContinuous Ab.{max u v}
        (topology B S hS 𝒳) (associatedTopology B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p B.topology)) := by
  have hR : ((objectProperty B S hS 𝒳).ι.sheafPushforwardContinuous Ab.{max u v}
      (topology B S hS 𝒳)
      (associatedTopology B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p B.topology)).IsRightAdjoint :=
    ⟨_, ⟨abelianShriekAdjunction.{u, w, v} B S hS 𝒳⟩⟩
  have hL : ((objectProperty B S hS 𝒳).ι.sheafPushforwardContinuous Ab.{max u v}
      (topology B S hS 𝒳)
      (associatedTopology B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p B.topology)).IsLeftAdjoint :=
    ⟨_, ⟨(objectProperty B S hS 𝒳).ι.sheafAdjunctionCocontinuous Ab.{max u v}
      (topology B S hS 𝒳) (associatedTopology B S hS 𝒳.val.val.p B.topology)⟩⟩
  exact (exactFunctor_iff _).2 ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩

section Modules

attribute [local instance] hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat

/-- **Lower shriek on sheaves of modules is additive.** `g_!` of **Stacks 0789** part (2) is a
left adjoint, so the same argument as for
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf.abelianShriek_additive` applies; the category of sheaves of
modules on the flat-fppf site is abelian because that site is essentially small.

This is what the total left derived functor `Lg_!` of **Stacks 07AS** part (4) needs of `g_!`. -/
theorem moduleShriek_additive : (moduleShriek.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳).Additive := by
  have : (moduleShriek.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳).IsLeftAdjoint :=
    ⟨_, ⟨moduleShriekAdjunction.{u, w} B S hS 𝒳⟩⟩
  exact additive_of_isLeftAdjoint _

end Modules

end AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.FlatFppf

end
